Report why cp could not remove an existing destination.
When the destination could not be created and then could not be
unlinked either, ask_and_unlink always printed the error from the first
attempt. For an existing destination that is EEXIST, so a destination
that could not be removed, such as a file in use, gave "can't create
'dst': File exists", which hides the real cause. Keep the first error
only when unlink says the destination does not exist, and otherwise
report the unlink error.

---
 libbb/copy_file.c |    5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/libbb/copy_file.c
+++ b/libbb/copy_file.c
@@ -60,7 +60,10 @@
 			return -1; /* error */
 		}
 #endif
-		errno = e; /* do not use errno from unlink */
+		/* If dest is not there, say why it could not be created;
+		 * else say why it could not be removed */
+		if (errno == ENOENT)
+			errno = e;
 		bb_perror_msg("can't create '%s'", dest);
 		return -1; /* error */
 	}
